 NEURALIS GEO

**AI Visibility Platform — built by [Neuralis Black](https://neuralisblack.com)**

Monitor and improve your brand's citation presence across AI-powered search engines: Perplexity, ChatGPT, and Claude. Built for European deep-tech startups in longevity, climate tech, and agentic AI.

---

## What it does

Neuralis GEO runs structured queries against three major LLM engines, detects whether your brand is cited, scores the result on a 0–100 GEO scale, and generates prioritised remediation recommendations. Scores are tracked over time and delivered as monthly email reports.

```
Brand URL + Vertical + Description
        ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  GEO AUDIT ENGINE                       │
│  5 queries × 3 LLMs = 15 data points   │
│  Anthropic · OpenAI · Perplexity        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
        ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  SCORING ALGORITHM                      │
│  Presence (40) + Coverage (25)          │
│  + Position (20) + Sentiment (15)       │
│  = GEO Score 0–100                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
        ↓
  Airtable (persistent storage)
        ↓
  Dashboard + Monthly Email Report
```

---

## GEO Score Tiers

| Tier  | Score  | Label     | Meaning |
|-------|--------|-----------|---------|
| GEO-5 | 85–100 | Dominant  | AI-citable across all major engines |
| GEO-4 | 65–84  | Strong    | Cited consistently, minor gaps |
| GEO-3 | 45–64  | Moderate  | Partial citation, improvement needed |
| GEO-2 | 25–44  | Weak      | Occasional citation, significant gaps |
| GEO-1 | 0–24   | Invisible | Not present in AI search index |

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer       | Technology |
|-------------|------------|
| Framework   | Next.js 14 (App Router) |
| Styling     | Tailwind CSS |
| Database    | Airtable |
| Auth        | NextAuth.js (magic link) |
| LLM APIs    | Anthropic, OpenAI, Perplexity |
| Charts      | Recharts |
| Email       | Nodemailer |
| Deployment  | Vercel (recommended) |
| Scheduler   | GitHub Actions |

---

## Quick Start

### 1. Clone and install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/neuralis-geo.git
cd neuralis-geo
npm install
```

### 2. Set up Airtable

Create a new Airtable base with four tables:

**Clients**
| Field | Type |
|-------|------|
| Name | Single line text |
| Email | Email |
| Brand | Single line text |
| URL | URL |
| Vertical | Single line text |
| Description | Long text |
| Plan | Single select: starter, pro, agency |
| Active | Checkbox |
| Created | Date |
| LastAudit | Date |

**Audits**
| Field | Type |
|-------|------|
| ClientId | Single line text |
| Brand | Single line text |
| AuditedAt | Date |
| DurationMs | Number |
| TotalQueries | Number |
| SuccessfulQueries | Number |
| RawResults | Long text |

**Scores**
| Field | Type |
|-------|------|
| ClientId | Single line text |
| AuditId | Single line text |
| Brand | Single line text |
| Score | Number |
| Tier | Single line text |
| TierLabel | Single line text |
| PresenceScore | Number |
| CoverageScore | Number |
| PositionScore | Number |
| SentimentScore | Number |
| CitationCount | Number |
| ScoredAt | Date |
| EngineBreakdown | Long text |

**Recommendations**
| Field | Type |
|-------|------|
| ClientId | Single line text |
| AuditId | Single line text |
| Priority | Number |
| Category | Single line text |
| Action | Long text |
| Impact | Single select: High, Medium, Low |
| Effort | Single select: Low, Medium, High |
| Rationale | Long text |
| Resolved | Checkbox |
| ResolvedAt | Date |

### 3. Configure environment

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
```

Fill in your keys:

```env
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
OPENAI_API_KEY=...
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=...
AIRTABLE_API_KEY=...        # Personal Access Token
AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=...        # From Airtable URL: airtable.com/BASEID/...
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=...         # openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
SMTP_HOST=smtp.zoho.com
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=you@yourdomain.com
SMTP_PASS=...
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
```

### 4. Run

```bash
npm run dev
```

Visit `http://localhost:3000/onboard` to create your first client.

---

## Routes

| Route | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `/onboard` | Self-serve client signup (3-step) |
| `/auth/signin` | Magic link sign-in |
| `/dashboard` | Client GEO monitoring dashboard |
| `POST /api/audit` | Trigger a GEO audit |
| `GET /api/dashboard` | Fetch dashboard data |
| `POST /api/clients` | Create a new client |
| `POST /api/reports` | Send monthly email report |
| `PATCH /api/recommendations/[id]` | Resolve a recommendation |

---

## Scheduler

### Manual audit (single client)
```bash
node scripts/run-audit.js --email client@company.com
```

### Manual audit (all clients)
```bash
node scripts/run-audit.js
```

### Dry run (no audit, list only)
```bash
node scripts/run-audit.js --dry-run
```

### Send reports manually
```bash
node scripts/send-reports.js
```

### GitHub Actions (automatic monthly)
Add secrets to your GitHub repo (`Settings → Secrets`):
- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `PERPLEXITY_API_KEY`
- `AIRTABLE_API_KEY`, `AIRTABLE_BASE_ID`
- `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`
- `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`

The workflow runs automatically on the 1st of every month at 06:00 UTC.
Manual trigger available via GitHub Actions UI.

---

## Deploy to Vercel

```bash
npm i -g vercel
vercel
```

Add all `.env.local` variables to Vercel's Environment Variables dashboard.

